ceived, even if i've asked it to seek.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/90533949/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"IanDBird","id":165482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQ4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird","html_url":"https://github.com/IanDBird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/90535577","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/385#issuecomment-90535577","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/385","id":90535577,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkwNTM1NTc3","user":{"login":"IanDBird","id":165482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQ4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird","html_url":"https://github.com/IanDBird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-04-07T12:43:04Z","updated_at":"2015-04-07T12:43:04Z","body":"I think the issue is that `ExoPlayerImplInteranl`'s `incrementalPrepareInternal` requires the track renderers to complete \"preparing\" before it begins playback. If you follow this, this means that the `MediaCodecTrackRenderer` call's it's Sources `source.prepare();` My understanding from reading `HlsSampleSource`'s prepare method is that it wont complete until it's read a chunk. So since it's not been told about the seek, it's attempting to grab the first chunk. If this isn't available, it will never complete. Hence why my hack is working around it by shifting which chunk it attempts to initially load when preparing.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/90535577/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"IanDBird","id":165482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTQ4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/165482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird","html_url":"https://github.com/IanDBird","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IanDBird/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/90574351","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/385#issuecomment-90574351","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/385","id":90574351,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDkwNTc0MzUx","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-04-07T14:09:23Z","updated_at":"2015-04-07T14:09:23Z","body":"Yeah, I see. So calling seekTo before prepare does work (i.e. the end result is playback starts from the position you're trying to start from). It's just that preparation fetches the first part of the first chunk, where-as it should be possible to prepare using the chunk you're actually trying to 